From: GPD XD+ TWRP device tree
Subject: [PATCH] openrecoveryscript: report wipe, format and CLI failures

A scripted wipe could not fail. Three layers each discarded the result:
openrecoveryscript.cpp ran Format_Data(), Factory_Reset(), Wipe_By_Path() and
Wipe_Dalvik_Cache() without looking at what they returned; Run_CLI_Command()
threw away run_script_file()'s value; and GUIAction::twcmd passed a literal 0 to
operation_end(). So `twrp format data` ended "Done processing script file" with
status 0 whether or not the partition was touched. The GUI wipe button was
unaffected -- it already passed its own ret_val to operation_end().

Propagate the status through all three. Note this cannot reach the `twrp`
binary's own exit code: orscmd talks to TWRP over a text-only FIFO and returns 0
regardless. What it does fix is the reported operation status and the
/cache/recovery/openrecoveryscript path, where Run_OpenRecoveryScript_Action()
reboots to system only when run_script_file() returned 0.

diff --git a/gui/action.cpp b/gui/action.cpp
index d5b8c8f..bddf720 100755
--- a/gui/action.cpp
+++ b/gui/action.cpp
@@ -1823,12 +1823,14 @@ int GUIAction::flashimage(std::string arg __unused)
 
 int GUIAction::twcmd(std::string arg)
 {
+	int op_status = 0;
+
 	operation_start("TWRP CLI Command");
 	if (simulate)
 		simulate_progress_bar();
 	else
-		OpenRecoveryScript::Run_CLI_Command(arg.c_str());
-	operation_end(0);
+		op_status = OpenRecoveryScript::Run_CLI_Command(arg.c_str());
+	operation_end(op_status);
 	return 0;
 }
 
